# The runtime dependencies, as ranges. EDIT THIS FILE, not requirements.txt.
#
# requirements.txt is generated from this file by pip-compile and pins every
# package, transitive ones included, with hashes. CI, the Hugging Face Space
# (Dockerfile), a Factory rebuild and the Glama release all install that file,
# so each of them runs the exact set the suite was proven on. Before the lock
# (decided 2026-09-29) every rebuild re-resolved these ranges against whatever
# PyPI served that day, and the test gate certified an environment production
# did not necessarily get.
#
# Regenerate after editing this file, on Python 3.13 (the Space's image), with
# the pip-tools that Dependabot runs:
#
#   pip install "pip-tools==7.5.3" "click<8.2"
#   pip-compile --generate-hashes --strip-extras --output-file requirements.txt requirements.in
#
# click<8.2 is not optional: with a newer click, pip-tools 7.5.3 writes a
# spurious --no-index into the command recorded in the lock's header, and that
# command then fails when it is re-run. Add --upgrade to move every pin to the
# newest versions these ranges allow; that is a deliberate refresh, delivered
# and tested like any other change. Dependabot (security updates only; see
# .github/dependabot.yml) regenerates the lock when a pinned package has an
# advisory.
#
# Engine, store, and resolver are standard-library only.
fastmcp>=3.4,<4
huggingface_hub>=1.0,<2

# Imported directly (pydantic in api.py and server.py, starlette in server.py),
# so declared rather than left to arrive through fastmcp: a refresh that
# dropped either would break an import.
pydantic>=2,<3
starlette>=1,<2
